    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Gate an AI agent's tools by flag\n\nA tool attached to an AI Agent node is always available to the model — there's no built-in way to show or hide one tool based on a condition. To gate a tool, evaluate a flag first and use an **If** node to route to one of two agents: one wired to only the tools you're comfortable the model always has (**Support agent (standard)**), the other wired to the same tools plus the one that takes a real action — here, sending an email (**Support agent (advanced)**). Turning the flag off removes the tool itself, not just a check the model could ignore or route around.\n\n**Setup:**\n1. Connect your own Unleash Frontend API token credential, and a Header Auth credential for the webhook.\n2. **Support agent (advanced)** only has its Gmail Tool wired here, to spotlight the gating — attach a Chat Model to it too, the same way **Support agent (standard)** has one, before you run this for real.\n3. Connect your own Gmail credential to **Send refund email**, and your own model credential to the Chat Model node(s) — Anthropic is shown here, swap for any model the AI Agent node supports.\n\nWorks on every Unleash plan — only needs a Frontend API token.\n\nUses the [@unleash/n8n-nodes-unleash](https://github.com/Unleash/n8n-nodes-unleash) community node (tested at v0.1.2) for **Evaluate a flag**. It's verified by n8n — install it directly from the canvas on n8n Cloud, or via [Community Nodes](https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/community-nodes/installation-and-management/gui-installation) on a self-hosted instance.",
        "height": 620,
        "width": 440
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [0, -560],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "342f2011-3047-4c67-98d4-9b5f4b4aed59",
      "name": "Sticky Note"
    }
